{"title":"Career Roadmap · Cinematographer","role":"Cinematographer","summary":"A Cinematographer (Director of Photography / DoP) is responsible for the visual language of a film or video production. The role combines camera operation, lighting, composition, lenses, movement, colour, visual storytelling and collaboration with the director to translate a creative vision into compelling images.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Film & Video Communication"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Approx. Years","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"2026–2027"},{"text":"Photography, composition, camera and lighting"}],[{"text":"Exploration"},{"text":"2027–2028"},{"text":"Camera operation, cinematography exercises"}],[{"text":"Portfolio"},{"text":"2028–2029"},{"text":"Short films, music videos, commercial projects"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"2029–2030"},{"text":"Camera/Lighting Assistant, Cinematography Intern"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Assistant Cinematographer / Junior DoP"}],[{"text":"Professional"},{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Independent Cinematographer / DoP"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"2037–2040"},{"text":"Senior DoP / Visual Storytelling Lead"}],[{"text":"Strategic"},{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Established DoP / Visual Director / Creative Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Visual & Camera Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong foundation in visual storytelling."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Photography"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Framing"},{"text":"Perspective"},{"text":"Visual balance"},{"text":"Colour theory"},{"text":"Light and shadow"},{"text":"Storyboarding"},{"text":"Shot design"},{"text":"Visual narrative"},{"text":"Film language"},{"text":"Basic editing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Camera fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exposure"},{"text":"ISO"},{"text":"Shutter speed"},{"text":"Aperture"},{"text":"White balance"},{"text":"Frame rate"},{"text":"Resolution"},{"text":"Dynamic range"},{"text":"Focus"},{"text":"Depth of field"},{"text":"Lens characteristics"},{"text":"Sensor formats"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Lenses"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand practical differences between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wide-angle"},{"text":"Normal"},{"text":"Telephoto"},{"text":"Prime"},{"text":"Zoom"},{"text":"Anamorphic lenses"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DaVinci Resolve"},{"text":"Adobe Premiere Pro"},{"text":"After Effects"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Lightroom"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Proof of learning"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"20–30 photography compositions"},{"text":"A visual storytelling photo series"},{"text":"A one-minute silent film"},{"text":"Shot breakdowns of professional films"},{"text":"Basic lighting experiments"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Cinematography Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from photography toward motion-picture cinematography."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Shot sizes"},{"text":"Camera angles"},{"text":"Camera movement"},{"text":"Blocking"},{"text":"Lens selection"},{"text":"Lighting ratios"},{"text":"Three-point lighting"},{"text":"Natural lighting"},{"text":"Motivated lighting"},{"text":"Practical lighting"},{"text":"Colour temperature"},{"text":"Exposure management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Camera movement"},{"type":"p","text":"Practice:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Static shots"},{"text":"Pan"},{"text":"Tilt"},{"text":"Dolly"},{"text":"Tracking"},{"text":"Crane"},{"text":"Gimbal"},{"text":"Handheld"},{"text":"Steadicam-style movement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Lighting"},{"type":"p","text":